      "pins": ["FCC2.48", "FCC2.73", "NAVC2.31", "NAVC2.47"],
      "nets": ["NET0026", "NET0138", "NET0174", "NET0033"],
      "observed": "Both MCUs' VCAP pins lack the required external capacitors. The FCC VCAP pins are routed to the UART3_FCC2 connector, and NAVC2 VCAP_1 is routed to I2C3_NAVC2; neither MCU's VCAP pins are shown with the required decoupling capacitors.",
      "expected": "The STM32H753VITx and STM32F405RGTx VCAP pins should have the external capacitors required by their datasheets and should not be used as connector signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "VCAP pin 48 NET0026; VCAP pin 73 NET0138 (FCC sheet, page 2/6)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "UART3_FCC2 pins include NET0026 and NET0138 (FCC Peripherals sheet, page 5/6)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "VCAP_1 pin 31 NET0174; VCAP_2 pin 47 NET0033 (NAVC sheet, page 3/6)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "I2C3_NAVC2 connector includes NET0174 (NAVC Peripherals sheet, page 6/6)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "FCC: STM32H753VITx; NAVC: STM32F405RGTx (§2 Component Table)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The internal core regulator supply may not operate correctly, preventing one or both MCUs from starting or functioning reliably. Routing these supply pins to connectors also risks loading or driving them as if they were GPIO signals.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic leaves the VCAP pins of both MCUs without required external capacitors, and routes several of those pins to connector nets. This is a serious power-integrity and MCU-operation defect."
}

